            against libpam.so.0 on Linux.

        * Bug fix: harden SSL/TLS session-cache-disabled mode and expired
          client-certificate handling against uninitialized-cache and stale
          peer-certificate hazards (Oracle 13725520, 16834733).

            When <ssl-session-cache><enabled>false</enabled></ssl-session-cache>
            is configured in server.xml, servssl_init_early() and
            servssl_init_late() skip SSL_ConfigMPServerSIDCache() and
            SSL_ConfigServerSessionIDCache(), leaving NSS's globalCache
            uninitialized.  servssl_init_late() in src/server/base/servnss.cpp
            now sets SSL_OptionSetDefault(SSL_NO_CACHE, PR_TRUE) whenever
            Vssl_cache_entries == 0, SSLSocketConfiguration::enableSSL() in
            src/server/base/sslconf.cpp preserves prior SSL_OptionSet() failure
            statuses across SSL_NO_STEP_DOWN and SSL_BYPASS_PKCS11 calls, and
            servssl_check_session(), get_auth_user_ssl(), pcheck_ssl_check(),
