            Vssl_cache_entries > 0.  INTsession_fill_ssl() in
            src/server/base/session.cpp and auth_get_sslid() in
            src/server/safs/auth.cpp now guard BTOA_DataToAscii() against
            0-length session IDs (which otherwise set SEC_ERROR_INVALID_ARGS in
            thread-local NSPR error state).  In src/server/safs/clauth.cpp,
            when an on-demand client-certificate handshake (ca_GetClientCert())
            fails (such as when a client presents an expired certificate, where
            NSS populates ss->sec.peerCert before ssl3_AuthCertificate()
            rejects the certificate), the session is marked failed and
            keep-alive is disabled so subsequent CA_GetClientCert() calls on
            the same request cannot accept the unverified certificate.

        * Bug fix / enhancement: enable client-certificate authentication on
          TLS-only listeners (<ssl3>false</ssl3>), support TLS 1.3
          post-handshake client authentication (dorequest="1"), and propagate
          TLS session and peer-certificate state to HTTP/2 streams
