            CA_getcert() and ca_GetClientCert() in src/server/safs/clauth.cpp
            previously gated PathCheck fn="get-client-cert" (and ACL
            get_user_cert_ssl()) on sslc->ssl3, rejecting client-certificate
            authentication with HTTP4034 whenever <ssl3>false</ssl3> was
            configured on a TLS 1.2/1.3 listener.  Both functions now accept
            listeners with either sslc->ssl3 or sslc->tls enabled, and
            conf_init_true_globals() / conf_get_globals() in
            src/server/frame/conf.cpp now set Vssl3_active from
            (ssl3 || tls) and Vssl2_active from ssl2.  For on-demand
            dorequest="1" requests in ca_GetClientCert(), TLS 1.3 connections
            now use NSS post-handshake authentication via
            SSL_SendCertificateRequest() while TLS 1.2 connections continue to
            use SSL_ReHandshakeWithTimeout(), and HTTP/2 streams reject
            mid-connection renegotiation per RFC 9113 section 9.2.1.  For
            HTTP/2 over TLS, H2Session::init() captures the negotiated cipher,
            key sizes, session ID, and peer certificate from the underlying TLS
            socket and H2Stream::fillSSLSession() populates rqSn.sn.client and
            cla->cla_cert on each dispatched stream so <client-auth> and
            get-client-cert work over HTTP/2.

2026-10-16  Joe McCabe <joe@jmccabe.org>

        * Bug fix: harden outbound reverse-proxy TLS channel, fix TLS 1.2/1.3
          origin client-certificate authentication, and disable SSLv2-compatible
          ClientHello encoding (Oracle 22280443, 20852421).

            enable_ssl() in src/server/libproxy/channel.cpp previously
            configured outbound proxy sockets with legacy
            SSL_OptionSet(fd, SSL_ENABLE_SSL2/SSL_ENABLE_SSL3/SSL_ENABLE_TLS, PR_TRUE)
            calls and only invoked SSL_SetURL() when validate_server_cert was
            enabled.  On NSS 3.x, the legacy SSL_ENABLE_SSL3 / SSL_ENABLE_TLS
            option calls expand the socket's protocol version range down to
            SSL 3.0 / TLS 1.0, and omitting SSL_SetURL() when
            validate-server-cert="false" suppressed the TLS SNI extension on
            outbound ClientHello messages.  enable_ssl() now explicitly
            disables SSL_ENABLE_SSL2 and SSL_V2_COMPATIBLE_HELLO, enforces
            SSL_LIBRARY_VERSION_TLS_1_2 .. SSL_LIBRARY_VERSION_TLS_1_3 via
            SSL_VersionRangeSet(), sets SSL_SetPKCS11PinArg(), and always
            calls SSL_SetURL() so SNI is sent regardless of server certificate
            validation mode.  get_client_cert_and_key() now uses
            servnss_get_cert_from_nickname() and PK11_FindPrivateKeyFromCert()
            with token:nickname slot support before falling back to
            CERT_FindCertByNickname() / PK11_FindKeyByAnyCert().

        * Bug fix / enhancement: prevent false offline marking of healthy
          reverse-proxy origin servers and make the offline-origin probe
          interval configurable (Oracle 23495921, 6933187).

            httpclient_process() and http_processor() in
            src/server/libproxy/httpclient.cpp previously treated single-request
            response header read timeouts, mid-body errors, and initial failures
            on reused or single-retry connections as hard server failures that
            immediately invoked route_offline(), marking healthy origin servers
            offline across the virtual server.  http_processor() now
            distinguishes response-stage errors and slow-request read timeouts
            (HTTP_PROCESSOR_RESPONSE_FAILURE) from connection-establishment
            failures, and httpclient_process() only marks an origin offline via
            route_offline() when channel_acquire() cannot establish a
            connection to the origin.  In src/server/libproxy/route.cpp,
            check_http_server() now attaches virtual-server objects whose Route
            directives reference the probed gateway (so ssl-client-config and
            http-client-config directives in named objects apply during health
            probes), preserves the canonical gateway URL in rq->vars["path"]
            and rq->vars["escaped"], and treats PROTOCOL_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT (504)
            as an offline response alongside PROTOCOL_BAD_GATEWAY (502) and
            PROTOCOL_REQUEST_TIMEOUT (408).  route_offline_thread() now probes
            offline gateways on every interval regardless of whether new traffic
            arrived since the prior pass, and the probe interval is configurable
            via <offline-check-interval> in schema/heliod-web-server_1_0.xsd
            (default 30 seconds, dynamically reconfigurable),
            OfflineCheckInterval in magnus.conf, or offline-check-interval on
            set-origin-server / set-proxy-server.

        * Bug fix: harden 64-bit va_list handling and buffer bounds across
          NSAPI error logging and formatting APIs (log_error_v, ereport_v,
          util_vsnprintf, util_vsprintf, and NsprError).

            Under the 32-bit x86 and SPARC ABIs this codebase was originally
            written for, va_list was a scalar pointer passed by value, so
            passing a va_list to util_vsnprintf(), util_vsprintf(), or
            log_error_v() left the caller's va_list intact for subsequent
            formatting or logging calls.  Under the 64-bit System V AMD64 ABI,
            va_list is a 1-element struct array (struct __va_list_tag[1]) that
            decays to a pointer, so PR_vsnprintf() mutates the caller's
            va_list register/stack offsets in place and any second use by the
            server or a third-party NSAPI SAF reads garbage off the stack and
            crashes with SIGSEGV.  util_vsnprintf(), util_vsprintf()
            (src/server/base/util.cpp), and log_error_v()
            (src/server/frame/log.cpp) now format against a va_copy() of the
            incoming va_list so callers' va_list state is never clobbered,
            and util_snprintf() / util_sprintf() now pair va_start() with
            va_end().  Also fixes _setErrorv() in
            src/support/NsprWrap/NsprError.cpp, which previously passed an
            already-consumed va_list to variadic PR_smprintf(fmt, args)
            instead of PR_vsmprintf() with a va_copy() when formatting error
            messages longer than 255 bytes, and hardens log_error_v() and
            _ereport_vsprintf() (src/server/base/ereport.cpp) against NULL
            Session / Request / client-IP pointers and buffer truncation
            overflow.

        * Bug fix: fix crash in reverse-proxy error logging and error page
          generation (Oracle 6981086).

            agent_error() in src/server/libproxy/proxyerror.cpp previously
            formatted the proxy error description into msg with
            PR_vsnprintf(msg, MAX_MSG_LEN, fmt, args) and then called
            log_error_v(degree, fn, sn, rq, fmt, args) with the already-
            consumed va_list, crashing on 64-bit x86_64 whenever degree (such
            as LOG_FAILURE) was active.  agent_error() now logs the
            already-formatted msg buffer via log_error(..., "%s", msg).
            Also removes the #ifdef FEAT_PROXY guard that stubbed out
            proxyerror_magnus_internal_send_proxy_error() in standard builds,
            registers service-gateway-dump and service-channel-dump in
            src/server/frame/httpd-fn.cpp, HTML-escapes host in the
            PR_CONNECT_REFUSED_ERROR branch of proxyerror_channel_error(), and
            guards proxyerror.cpp and channel.cpp against NULL Session/Request
            pointers.

