2026-09-01  Joe McCabe <joe@jmccabe.org>

        * version 0.5

            Adds HTTP/2, an event-driven I/O model, hardened TLS, and
            modern content codings.  The NSS TLS stack and the
            existing request-handling model (acceptor threads,
            connection queue, DaemonSession worker threads and
            keep-alive poll threads) remain the defaults.

            TLS hardening (NSS): SSLv2 and SSLv3 code paths removed;
            TLS 1.2 minimum / TLS 1.3 maximum enforced with
            SSL_VersionRangeSet; cipher table rewritten around AEAD
            suites (ECDHE-RSA/ECDSA AES-GCM and ChaCha20-Poly1305)
            with RC4, 3DES and export-grade entries removed; ALPN
            negotiation (http/1.1, and h2 on event-model listeners) and
            SNI-based certificate
            selection via SSL_SNISocketConfigHook.  ALPN requires
            NSS 3.123 or later; the Debian build links NSS 3.127 from
            the SBC tree (NSS_LIBDIR in defines_Linux_debian.mk).

            Event-driven I/O model (opt-in): new EventLoop (epoll on
            Linux, kqueue on BSD/macOS, event ports on Solaris),
            WorkerPool and EventDispatcher in src/server/httpdaemon.
            Selected per listener with the new <io-model> element in
            server.xml, "classic" (the default, i.e. the existing
            model) or "event"; HELIOD_EVENT_MODEL /
            HELIOD_EVENT_IDLE_TIMEOUT environment overrides.  In the
            event model the acceptor threads hand new connections to
            an event loop, which takes the place of the connection
            queue and keep-alive poll threads: it watches idle
            keep-alive connections and dispatches ready connections
            to a worker pool that grows on demand from min-threads to
            max-threads.  As in the existing model, a worker thread
            holds a connection only while processing a request.

            HTTP/2 (RFC 9113) via nghttp2, on event-model listeners:
            negotiated through ALPN "h2" over TLS, plus cleartext h2c
            with prior knowledge (connection-preface detection).  The
            HTTP/1.1 Upgrade: h2c path and server push are not
            supported.  Each stream is dispatched through the normal
            NSAPI/SAF pipeline as a synthetic HTTP/1.1 request, so
            static files, CGI, FastCGI, ACLs and access logging work
            unchanged; split Cookie header fields (RFC 9113 8.2.3)
            are rejoined before dispatch.  Streams are processed from
            a shared worker pool rather than tying a thread to each
            connection; idle-connection timeout; h2spec conformance
            138/146.

            Compression: Brotli (br) and Zstandard (zstd) content
            codings added to the http-compression output filter
            alongside gzip, chosen by Accept-Encoding q-value with a
            br > zstd > gzip tie-break.  libnghttp2, libbrotlienc and
            libzstd are linked into libns-httpd40.so.

            perfdump gains an event-pool section and an "HTTP/2 (this
            process)" section with stream accounting, and lists
            event-model and HTTP/2 sessions.

            Build and test: libnghttp2, libbrotli and libzstd
            development packages are new build dependencies;
            create-instance and post-install are installed into the
            work bin so the smoke tests can create their own
            instance; test/TESTING.md added, along with smoke tests
            for TLS, event vs. classic I/O parity, HTTP/2 (basic,
            lifecycle, parallel streams, streaming responses, request
            end, idle timeout, cookies, client IP, FastCGI, h2spec,
            browser interop, h2 vs. HTTP/1.1 performance),
            compression and worker-pool growth.


2026-08-17  Joe McCabe <joe@jmccabe.org>

        * version 0.4

            Build support for Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (x86_64) with GCC/G++ 15,
            GNU Make 4.4 and current NSS, NSPR, Xerces-C, Xalan-C and
            MozLDAP 6.0.5.  Platform defaults now produce 64-bit
            binaries without BUILD64.

            Added BUILD.md with build instructions and dependencies,
            referencing the sbc/ helpers for building the SBC tree.

            Build system: sensible defaults for library suffixes,
            dynamic-link and PIC flags and compiler paths; Sun-style
            mapfiles disabled on Linux; position-independent code
            forced for all shared libraries and plugins; rpath-link
            entries for webservd; Debian LDAP SDK include layout
            (mozldap public headers and the MozLDAP source tree for
            ldap_ssl.h); Java source level raised to 8; Complex.cpp
            built at -O1 to avoid exhausting memory on low-RAM hosts.

            Modern toolchain compatibility: -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=0 and
            -D__NO_INLINE__ to work around legacy K&R variadic code and
            duplicate glibc stdio inline symbols; -fcommon and -fpermissive on Debian/Ubuntu;
            removed obsolete "auto" storage specifiers, const-
            correctness and type-mismatch fixes; header availability
            fixes (sys/ioctl.h, sys/stropts.h, errno.h, getopt.h for
            svrctl, crypt.h removal, LDAP_CALL/LDAP_CALLBACK fallbacks).

            Library API updates: NSPR input source and XML parser
            adjusted for Xerces-C 3.x (XMLSize_t/XMLFilePos,
            getContentType); NSS and Xalan type signature fixes; raw
            OpenLDAP calls switched to the ldapu_* wrappers.

            Runtime fixes for modern Linux: use close_range() in the
            CGI stub so fd cleanup is not pathologically slow under
            large RLIMIT_NOFILE; cap fd-based auto-sizing of the
            connection-queue, keep-alive and file-cache tables at
            65536 to avoid OOM at startup with very high ulimit -n;
            serialize crypt() calls now that crypt_r is no longer
            used; SEM_FLOCK semaphore grab reworked to retry on
            EINTR/EAGAIN; guard SSL_ImportFD() with NSS_IsInitialized()
            so servers started without TLS can still initialize NSS
            policy later; procfs and signal-handling fixes; missing
            return in ChildExec::_startListener().

            Bug fixes: parsexml PID_FILE/TEMP_DIR resolution restored
            by re-enabling SAX2 namespaces; null-pointer checks in
            servact_uri2path, servact_lookup and control_dashu;
            libsed.h extern "C" brace mismatch; HP-UX added to the
            temp-file path logic.

            New feature: opt-in reverse-proxy client IP attribution
            for logging and perfdump.  New magnus.conf directives
            ReverseProxyIPHeader, ReverseProxyTrustedIPs (IPv4/IPv6
            addresses or CIDR ranges) and ReverseProxyLogAttribution
            (actual|proxied-ip|both), with a per-virtual-server
            <reverse-proxy> element in server.xml that can override
            them.  When a request arrives from a trusted proxy the
            forwarded client IP is reported in the errors log and in
            a new perfdump "Reported Client" column; the authoritative
            client IP used for ACLs and security is unchanged.

            General cleanup pass removing dead code and cruft; smoke
            test harness updated so "make -C test" runs after the
            build; .gitignore additions.


